{"question_id": "V2-dev-LAW-en-T3-002", "approach": "B1", "approach_base": "B1", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "L", "corpus_set": "LAW_en", "answer_text": "Bribery Act 2010 – 2010 CHAPTER 23: Failure of commercial organisations to prevent bribery – 7 Failure of commercial organisations to prevent bribery: A person guilty of an offence under section 7 is liable on conviction on indictment to a fine.  \nModern Slavery Act 2015 – 2015 CHAPTER 30: PART 6 Transparency in supply chains etc – 54 Transparency in supply chains etc: The duties imposed on commercial organisations by this section are enforceable by the Secretary of State bringing civil proceedings in the High Court for an injunction or, in Scotland, for specific performance of a statutory duty under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988.  \n\nThe Bribery Act offence is a criminal offence punishable by a fine. The Modern Slavery Act duty is not a criminal offence; it is enforced through civil proceedings for injunctions or specific performance.", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 156 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o012", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b99"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 0, "span": [9154, 9310], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 98 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o017", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b155"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 1, "span": [16249, 16347], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 155 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o012", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b102"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 2, "span": [9428, 9583], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 151 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en", "section_i